  "narrative": "The analysis examined whether late\u2011night phone use is associated with gambling expenditure. An initial request for monthly mean stakes broken down by night\u2011time phone\u2011use band was denied because the query omitted the month grouping (step\u202f1). A subsequent request for the same breakdown was fulfilled after redaction, releasing a table of mean stakes for each month and use band (step\u202f2). In month\u202f7, the released means were: heavy use\u202f=\u202f89.96\u202fGBP, regular use\u202f=\u202f27.15\u202fGBP, occasional use\u202f=\u202f18.42\u202fGBP, and rare use\u202f=\u202f14.27\u202fGBP, showing a gradient of higher stakes with more intense late\u2011night phone use. A separate analysis reported a small but statistically significant positive correlation between the number of late\u2011night phone\u2011use sessions and monthly gambling stake (step\u202f3): correlation\u202f=\u202f0.0817, p\u202f=\u202f0.0, based on n\u202f=\u202f72\u202f000. The authors note that the association is modest and that causality cannot be inferred from these observational aggregates.",
